# Reference only: the Worker does not load this file automatically.
# Set these values privately through your hosting provider's server-only runtime settings.
# Trusted server-only role/bootstrap configuration, not a membership allowlist.
# Replace the owner placeholder for YOUR deployment. Member entries are optional:
# new verified ChatGPT/Google identities register automatically as Signed up members.
# Owner Settings selects Inactive / Signed up / Active; only Active has full access.
# Removing an owner grant downgrades the role without changing account state.
# Sign-in, linking and bootstrap never elevate an existing account state.
# Only a new configured owner bootstraps Active; new configured members are Signed up.
# Keep a valid configured owner; the account-state control cannot demote an owner.
AUTHORIZED_ACCOUNTS='[{"email":"owner@example.invalid","role":"owner"},{"email":"member@example.invalid","role":"member"}]'
# Optional comma-separated exact HTTPS origins, only after verifying the receiver.
# https://chatgpt.com is already allowed by the application.
MCP_CALLBACK_ORIGINS=
# DB is a D1 binding, not a string environment variable.
# DOTCORD_TOKEN belongs only in the sender's private environment. Do not put a token here.

# Optional Google/Gmail sign-in fallback. Owners can instead configure this once
# in Dotcord Settings. Members never enter these application credentials.
# Create a Google Cloud OAuth Web application client.
# Configure its consent audience and authorize the exact deployed HTTPS callback.
# Saved owner configuration takes precedence. Never commit real credentials here.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://YOUR-SITE-HOST/auth/google/callback
# Requests openid email only. Gmail data access is not required.
# The host access policy and trusted identity-header boundary still apply.
# AUTHORIZED_ACCOUNTS grants roles; Google members do not need an entry.
